# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# IDE
.vs/
*.user
*.suo

# Local Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Published self-contained hook binaries (e.g. hooks/AgentSchemaGuard/publish/*.exe) —
# regenerable via `dotnet publish`, not committed since a self-contained win-x64 build is
# ~70MB and not delta-friendly across rebuilds. See CLAUDE.md for the one-time build step.
hooks/*/publish/

# npx-skills-installed content: .agents/skills/<name> is the canonical store, and
# .claude/skills/<name> for an installed (not hand-authored) skill is meant to be a
# symlink into it. This checkout has core.symlinks=false, so git would otherwise walk
# through the symlink and commit a full duplicate copy of the content at both paths.
# skills-lock.json (tracked) is what makes `npx skills add` reproduce these locally —
# regenerate rather than commit the copies themselves.
.agents/
.claude/skills/architecture/
.claude/skills/modern-csharp/

# Secrets — never commit these; use `dotnet user-secrets` instead
.env
.env.*
